\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Replay pool}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{replay}

\p{At accepted-update index #{n}, a \strong{replay pool}
#{\mathcal B_n} is a finite collection of immutable rollout records. A pool
update can insert newly generated records or retire existing records. It does
not alter a retained record.}

\p{Replay buffers are standard in off-policy reinforcement learning; see the
overview in \citef{murphy2024reinforcement}. The present definition is an FTIP
specialization to stamped language-model rollouts. It leaves the insertion,
eviction, and sampling policy explicit rather than identifying the pool with a
training minibatch.}

\p{A record can remain in the pool after the current policy has changed. Its
fitness for another update is evaluated by the selection step below.}
